1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,804
Here's a listing you might scroll past any day.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,021
A baby sleeper. Barely used.

3
00:00:05,021 --> 00:00:07,168
Twenty-five dollars, pickup only.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,181
It looks perfectly safe. But what if it isn't?

5
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,703
This is the Fisher-Price Rock 'n Play.

6
00:00:14,703 --> 00:00:18,317
In 2019 it was recalled, about 4.7 million units,

7
00:00:18,317 --> 00:00:20,604
after reports of infant deaths.

8
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:25,217
Inclined infant sleepers like it are now banned from sale entirely.

9
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,201
But a recall stops new sales, not resales.

10
00:00:28,201 --> 00:00:30,761
And this listing never says “Rock 'n Play.”

11
00:00:30,761 --> 00:00:32,249
It says “sleeper/rocker.”

12
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,640
This year, Consumer Reports found banned baby gear listed on every

13
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,560
major resale platform it checked.

14
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:41,087
So we built SecondLook.

15
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,700
A safety check for the moment before you buy something used.

16
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,405
Paste a listing, or snap the label.

17
00:00:47,405 --> 00:00:50,496
It checks U.S. recalls and federal sale bans,

18
00:00:50,496 --> 00:00:53,107
then tells you what to ask the seller.

19
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:58,033
Here's that same listing, pasted in exactly as the seller wrote it.

20
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,461
The verdict: don't buy this.

21
00:01:02,461 --> 00:01:06,979
Inclined sleepers are banned, and it matches the actual CPSC recall.

22
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:15,233
Sellers often send a photo of the label instead.

23
00:01:15,233 --> 00:01:17,712
SecondLook reads it right in your browser.

24
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:23,949
It picks up the brand and the model number, and runs the same check.

25
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,042
Many recalls are narrower.

26
00:01:27,042 --> 00:01:29,631
This infant swing matches a 4moms recall,

27
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:31,715
but only some models are covered.

28
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,688
So SecondLook writes the questions for you,

29
00:01:34,688 --> 00:01:36,829
ready to copy and send to the seller.

30
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,395
And it shows exactly which models the notice covers.

31
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,603
For thrift stores and donation drives,

32
00:01:44,603 --> 00:01:49,125
batch mode screens a whole intake list at once, and exports a CSV.

33
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:56,530
Under the hood: 7,192 CPSC recalls, indexed,

34
00:01:56,530 --> 00:02:02,169
plus newer recalls pulled live from the public CPSC API.

35
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:06,566
A matching engine translates listing slang into recall language,

36
00:02:06,566 --> 00:02:09,164
resolves brands, and matches model numbers.

37
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:13,442
Federal bans are explicit rules with legal citations.

38
00:02:13,442 --> 00:02:17,395
The live app runs entirely on this deterministic engine,

39
00:02:17,395 --> 00:02:20,431
and every match links back to its evidence.

40
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:24,523
Before you buy it. Before you sell it. Look twice.

41
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,863
SecondLook. Free, and live today.
